depgraph: remember _select_atoms_probe results while _slot_operator_trigger_reinstalls runs

Sub-series: A (probe, match and config memos) - patch 1 of 10; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: unchanged (line numbers only)

_slot_operator_trigger_reinstalls probes every slot-operator dependency up
to twice, and each probe runs dep_check over all dependency strings of a
candidate parent. Dependencies that share a parent ask the same question
again (39,858 calls with 7,517 distinct arguments per loop on the largest
state). The loop writes only _backtrack_infos and _need_restart, which the
probe does not read, so within one call the probe is a function of
(root, pkg). The memo is dropped when the loop ends.

Alone on 3.0.83, resolve seconds stock -> patched:
  start 121.4 -> 108.3, holds 44.1 -> 36.8, masks 93.5 -> 75.2,
  py313 73.3 -> 66.5, bdeps 68.5 -> 49.8, policykit 46.7 -> 36.3
  sum of six 447.5 -> 372.7 (-17 %)
Lock-step check (memo hit recomputed the original way and compared):
63,455 hits on three states, 0 mismatches.
Applies to upstream head 2237c14dd unchanged; there 114.4 -> 102.5 s on start.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
---
--- a/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
+++ b/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
@@ -888,6 +888,8 @@
 
         self._virt_deps_visible_recursion = set()
         self._virtual_cycle = None
+        # Only set while _slot_operator_trigger_reinstalls runs.
+        self._probe_memo = None
 
     def _index_binpkgs(self):
         for root in self._frozen_config.trees:
@@ -3239,6 +3241,16 @@
         return available_pkg is not None
 
     def _select_atoms_probe(self, root, pkg):
+        memo = self._probe_memo
+        if memo is None:
+            return self._select_atoms_probe_imp(root, pkg)
+        key = ("select_atoms", root, pkg)
+        result = memo.get(key)
+        if result is None:
+            result = memo[key] = self._select_atoms_probe_imp(root, pkg)
+        return result
+
+    def _select_atoms_probe_imp(self, root, pkg):
         selected_atoms = []
         use = self._pkg_use_enabled(pkg)
         for k in pkg._dep_keys:
@@ -3380,6 +3392,20 @@
         rebuilds if they can link to a newer slot that's in the graph.
         """
 
+        # The loop below probes every slot operator dep twice, and deps that
+        # share a parent or a child repeat the same sub-probes many times.
+        # Nothing that runs inside the loop changes what the probes read: it
+        # only adds to _backtrack_infos and sets _need_restart. So during
+        # this call a repeated probe can be answered from a memo, which is
+        # dropped when the loop is done.
+        memo_backup = self._probe_memo
+        self._probe_memo = {}
+        try:
+            self._slot_operator_trigger_reinstalls_imp()
+        finally:
+            self._probe_memo = memo_backup
+
+    def _slot_operator_trigger_reinstalls_imp(self):
         rebuild_if_new_slot = (
             self._dynamic_config.myparams.get("rebuild_if_new_slot", "y") == "y"
         )
